cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Building an Equitable Network Growth (ENG) Corridor on MBTA Bus
  Routes 23, 28 and 66
message: If you use this analysis, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Anushri
    family-names: Gade
  - given-names: Rahul
    family-names: Tejannavar
  - given-names: Sahil
    family-names: Mittal
repository-code: "https://github.com/sahilmittal-policy/mbta-equity-corridors"
abstract: >-
  A data-driven case for targeted bus-priority investment on the three
  highest equity-volume corridors in the MBTA bus network. Builds a
  Transit Dependence Index from census demographics within route
  catchments, ranks routes by transit dependence weighted by ridership,
  measures the resulting service deficit from observed runtimes and
  on-time performance, and prices a quick-build bus-priority package
  that pays back in under two years. Second place, MIT Policy Hackathon
  2025 (Transportation track).
keywords:
  - transit equity
  - public transportation
  - bus priority
  - cost-benefit analysis
  - MBTA
  - policy analysis
license: MIT
date-released: "2025-11-23"
